  "discussion": "The current medium period northwest swell will linger today, holding surf to near near or slightly above seasonal average for north and west facing shores, before declining tonight through Friday. By late Friday, a medium period north- northwest swell will build and once again help bring surf back to near seasonal averages through the weekend. The current medium period south swell will keep surf along south facing shores elevated today. A reinforcing long period south swell will help produce surf near seasonal average tonight into early this weekend. Surf along east facing shores will remain small through Thursday as small wind waves and tiny east swell persist. Choppy surf will increase slightly as trade winds strengthen across the region Friday into the weekend.",
